// Targets a dying ALLY (a "stabilize" effect), not the caster -- `SelfBuff`
// always lands its effect on the caster (`entity: data.entity` in
// common/src/states/self_buff.rs), never a touched ally, so this uses
// `BasicMelee` with the engine's established touch-ally pattern (see
// weave_transfusion.ron / lesser_restoration.ron): a near-inert Stab whose
// `attack_effect_target: InGroup` redirects the effect onto whoever is
// struck instead of dealing damage. No dedicated "downed/dying" state
// exists in this engine (0 HP has no separate stabilize-able state), so the
// stabilize effect is modeled as a modest instant heal on the touched ally --
// the closest existing primitive to "pulls someone back from the brink"
// (see CombatEffect::Heal, common/src/combat.rs).
BasicMelee(
    energy_cost: 20.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    swing_duration: 0.1,
    hit_timing: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    melee_constructor: (
        kind: Stab(damage: 1, poise: 0, knockback: 0, energy_regen: 0),
        range: 3.0,
        angle: 20.0,
        attack_effect: Some((
            Heal(20.0),
            AttackSource(Melee),
        )),
        attack_effect_target: Some(InGroup),
    ),
    meta: (school: Some(Necromancy), source: Some(Divine)),
)
